From d4146470c2bf41305de59fad9a4788864e29a932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:40:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] iio: qcom-smgr: use 32-bit QMI length fields

In a buffering request that put the sensor ID and data type into the top bytes
of the item count. The accelerometer has ID 0 and data type 0, so its request
passed by luck. Every other sensor failed with "qmi_encode: Invalid data
length" and -EINVAL, so gyro, magnetometer, proximity, pressure and light could
not be read through the driver. On the decode side each reply overwrote the
three bytes after every length field.

Make the fields u32 and set elem_size to sizeof(u8) to keep them one byte on
the wire. This is what made the request fail in the previous lock fix.

Also stop a delete request recording a sample rate of 0, which left
in_accel_sampling_frequency reading 0 after the first stop.

Fixes: 0dc098dab0b0 ("iio: Add Qualcomm Sensor Manager driver")
Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
